ogical sample. It has been used as an iron chelator to grow plants without Fe-EDTA (ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid).\nL116: ### Biochem/physiol Actions\nL117: \nL118: Bathophenanthrolinedisulfonic acid is a metal chelator. It permits iron determination to be made in aqueous medium without need for solvent extraction. It forms a complex with Fe^{2+} and makes it unavailable to Fe^{2+} transporter, thereby inhibiting the transport of iron into chloroplasts. Bathophenanthrolinedisulfonic acid is also used in the assay for determining intracellular glutathione.\nL119: \nL120: * * *\nL121: \nL122: * * *\nL123: \nL124: ## Safety Information\nL125: \nL126: ### Storage Class\nL127: \nL128: 11 - Combustible Solids\nL129: ### WGK\nL130: \nL131: WGK 3\nL132: \nL133: ### Flash Point (°F)\nL134: \nL135: Not applicable\nL136: \nL137: ### Flash Point (°C)\nL138: \nL139: Not applicable\nL140: \nL141: ### PPE (personal protective equipment)\nL142: \nL143: Eyeshields, Gloves, type N95 (US)\nL144: \nL145: * * *\nL146: \nL147: ## Documentation\nL148: \nL149: Certificate of Analysis[Button: Certificate of Origin]\nL150: \nL151: * * *\nL152: \nL153: Choose from one of the most recent versions:\nL154: ### Certificates of Analysis (COA)\nL155: \nL156: Lot/Batch Number\nL157: \nL158: * * *\nL159: \nL160: Don't see the Right Version?\nL161: \nL162: If you require a particular version, you can look up a specific certificate by the Lot or Batch number.\nL163: \nL164: 【11†Search for a COA】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCefsulodin third-generation cephalosporin antibiotic 52152-93-9 (https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/PT/en/product/sigma/c8145)\nciteturn49view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn43view1\",\"pattern\":\"anhydrous basis\"}); Total lines: 406\nL36: ### Key Documents\nL37: \nL38:   * 【8†COA】\nL39: \nL40:   * 【8†COO】\nL41: \nL42: 【8†View All Documentation】\nL43: \nL44: ### Skip To\n